      "text": "VT-86\nCDR J. V. Seida SABREHAWKS CDR A. M. Farina\nCOMMANDING OFFICER EXECUTIVE OFFICER\nNAS PENSACOLA, FL\n\"TRAINING NFOs FOR THE WORLD\"\nFriday, 06-Nov-2026\nSUNRISE: 0608 MOONRISE: 0337 % ILLUM: 9% JULIAN DATE: 6310\nSUNSET: 1658 MOONSET: 1515\nTOTAL FLY EVENTS: 20 TOTAL FLY HRS: 24.5 SYL FLY EVENTS: 15 SYL FLY HRS: 16.7\nTOTAL SIM EVENTS: 0 TOTAL SIM HRS: 0.0 SYL SIM EVENTS: 0 SYL SIM HRS: 0.0\nCOMMANDER\u2019S COMMENTS:\nPENSACOLA CDO AND SDO SHALL BE AVAILABLE FOR RECALL\nQUESTIONS OF THE DAY:\nEP OF THE DAY: ABORT\nT-45 NATOPS: LIST 2 PROHIBITED MANEUVERS LISTED IN THE T-45C NATOPS.\nSOP: WHAT IS THE MAXIMUM TAXI SPEED ON A TAXIWAY?\nGK: DISCUSS DEPARTURE WEATHER REQUIREMENTS.\nDUTY/WATCH ASSIGNED SIGN IN SIGN OUT\nFLT Schedules Officer RUFF J 0700 1600\nCDO MARTENS N 0700 1600\nSDO Driscoll B 0600 1800\nDET CDO 1 RUFF J 0700 1200\nDET CDO 2 STEVENS J 1200 1800\nDET SDO Fails M 0700 1800\nFUTURE OPS:\nNOVEMBER 12: IGS NOVEMBER 25: SAFETY STAND DOWN\nNOVEMBER 17: INSTRUCTOR BCA DECEMBER 10: IGS\nNOVEMBER 17-19: FLEET FLY IN DECEMBER 11: HOLIDAY PARTY\nNOVEMBER 18: STUDENT MAKE UP PRT DECEMBER 17: IGS\nNOVEMBER 19: IGS\nNOVEMBER 20: INSTRUCTOR PRT\nSCHEDULE NOTES:\nALL HANDS SHALL PT EVERY WORKDAY IAW OPNAVINST 6110.0L\nUNDERLINED NAMES INDICATE CREW DAY >9 HRS ITALICIZED NAMES INDICATE STUDENTS SCHEDULED FOR TWO GRADED EVENTS\nAVN 4101/4102 AUTHORIZED FOR BACKUP EVENTS\n1. OUT/IN FLIGHTS\n2. OPTIONAL WARMUP\n3. VMTS A/C REQUIRED\n4. COMPLETE STAN EXAM PRIOR TO FLIGHT (INSTRUCTOR ONLY)\n5. STUDENT COMPLETION EVENT\n6. BLUES PRACTICE 1030-1130 NO TAXI AFTER 1015\n7. LL/BFM\n8. LOG A MINIMUM OF 1 HRS OF NIGHT TIME FOR STUDENT/PILOT\n9. INSTRUCTOR IAE REQUIRED\n10. INSTRUCTOR FINI FLIGHT"
